/* A physical product ships unless its seller turns "This product is shipped" off in the product editor: `products.requires_shipping` now defaults to true, as the editor, the shop and the checkout already read a product that never said. It was false since part 78, so a physical product whose row was written without the editor's shipping card (a save that stopped part way, an import, an agent) sold with no address, no shipping and no delivery at checkout. No rows change: a seller's own choice is kept. To see physical products that are not shipped, run: select id, title from public.products where type = 'physical' and requires_shipping = false; and turn "This product is shipped" on for the ones that should ship. Needs part 78. Safe to run again. */
ALTER TABLE public.products ALTER COLUMN requires_shipping SET DEFAULT true;
notify pgrst, 'reload schema';
